Description: An R interface to Jump-Switch-Flow ('JSF'), a hybrid
    simulation framework for compartmental reaction models that combines
    stochastic jump dynamics at low population sizes with deterministic flow
    dynamics at high population sizes. Simulations are performed using the
    Python 'jsf' backend through 'reticulate', with structured R outputs for
    inspection, summarization, and plotting. The underlying methodology is
    described in Germano et al. (2026) <doi:10.1007/s00285-026-02409-y>.
